# MIN-SR-S diagonal coefficients from Čaklović, Lunet, Götschel and Ruprecht,
# "Improving efficiency of parallel across the method spectral deferred
# corrections", SIAM J. Sci. Comput. 47 (2025) A430-A453, Definition 2.11: the diagonal entries that make
# the stiff-limit iteration matrix `I - QΔ⁻¹Q` nilpotent.
#
# They come from a numerical solve of that nilpotency condition seeded
# incrementally in `M`, not from a closed form, so they are tabulated rather than
# derived here. Generated with qmat's `MIN_SR_S` and checked against it in
# test/sdc_diagonal_sweeper_tests.jl.
# The residual spectral radius grows with `M` — about 1e-8 at M = 2 and 1e-1 at
# M = 10 — because the paper offers no guarantee that an exact solution exists.
